# beta-tester credentials — SCHEMA ONLY, placeholders, safe to commit.
#
# The real file lives OUTSIDE every repo. The skill takes the first of these that exists:
#
#     $BETA_TESTER_ENV        an override; if set it must exist
#     $HOME/.beta-tester.env  the default
#
# chmod 0600 — the skill refuses to run if the file is group- or world-readable.
#
# A path inside a project's own repo is never consulted, deliberately: a repo can be writable by
# the running application, cleaned, or checked out onto a branch that overwrites a file that
# ships inside it. Keep real values somewhere none of that can reach.
#
# Copy this schema to the resolved path and fill in real values. Never commit the real file, and
# never let the skill print an _EMAIL, _PASSWORD, or _API_TOKEN value — into the terminal, a
# report, or a filed task.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Schema
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#     BETA_TESTER_<PERSONA>_EMAIL
#     BETA_TESTER_<PERSONA>_PASSWORD
#     BETA_TESTER_<PERSONA>_API_TOKEN    optional, enables API mode for this persona
#     BETA_TESTER_<PERSONA>_LABEL        optional, one line, shown in the account picker
#
# <PERSONA>  a free identifier: DEFAULT, ADMIN, TRIAL, PAID, whatever the account is for in this
#            project.
#
# Personas are discovered by scanning key names, so adding an account here is the only step. The
# scan unions _EMAIL and _API_TOKEN, so a persona may be UI-only, API-only, or both — and it
# requires a NON-EMPTY value, so a placeholder like FOO_EMAIL="" is correctly treated as not
# configured rather than offered in the picker and then failing at login:
#
#     grep -oE '^BETA_TESTER_[A-Z0-9_]+_(EMAIL|API_TOKEN)=("[^"]+"|[^"[:space:]]+)' "$ENV_FILE" \
#       | sed -E 's/=.*$//; s/_(EMAIL|API_TOKEN)$//' | sort -u
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# _API_TOKEN's shape
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Auth shapes vary by target: a bearer header, a custom header pair, a query parameter, Basic
# auth. This file holds one credential value per persona; the skill asks once, at the start of
# the first API-mode run, how the target actually wants it sent, and remembers the answer for the
# rest of the run. Get the token however the target's own account/API-key settings issue one.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why more than one account
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Many products gate behaviour per account — a plan tier, a role, a feature flag. Testing a gated
# change as a plain account often doesn't fail loudly: it just exercises core behaviour and
# reports a clean pass. Configure one account per state you need to cover, and let the skill ask
# which to use.

# --- example accounts -------------------------------------------------------------------------

BETA_TESTER_DEFAULT_EMAIL=you@example.com
BETA_TESTER_DEFAULT_PASSWORD=change-me
BETA_TESTER_DEFAULT_API_TOKEN=change-me
BETA_TESTER_DEFAULT_LABEL=Plain account, no special entitlements

BETA_TESTER_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin-tester@example.com
BETA_TESTER_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me
BETA_TESTER_ADMIN_LABEL=Admin-role account — UI only, no API token

BETA_TESTER_PAID_EMAIL=paid-tester@example.com
BETA_TESTER_PAID_PASSWORD=change-me
BETA_TESTER_PAID_API_TOKEN=change-me
BETA_TESTER_PAID_LABEL=Paid-tier account with the gated feature set
